<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48263" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thymbra</span></b> , ae, or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thymbrē</span></b> , ēs,
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Θύμβρη,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a city in
			Troas</i>, <i>with a temple of Apollo</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 30,
				33, § 126</span></i> (dub.; al. Cambre); <i><span class="en">Stat. S. 4,
				7, 22</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thym-braeus</span></b> , i,
				m., <i>the Thymbræan</i>, an
			epithet of <i>Apollo</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 3,
				85</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">Macr. S. 1, 17</span></i>, and
				<i><span class="en">Fest. p. 356</span></i>
			Müll.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">thymbrae-um</span></b> , i,
				n., <i>another name for the</i>
			sisymbrium silvestre, <i><span class="en">Plin. 20, 22, 91, §
		247</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
